																		(Seeking Greenlight) The Uncontainable Man
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/damian-thorne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7106669); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7106669&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609202346" alt="Damian Thorne" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7106669)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/damian-thorne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7106669); return false;" >Damian Thorne</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609082596 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Dec 2020 15:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855100">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror, Drama/Emotional, Comedy, Action, History, Other (specify)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Alternating between versions of the Uncontainable Man's SCP file and prose sections detailing the Foundation's encounters with him.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A man who literally cannot be contained. If anyone tries to hold him against his will, <em>something</em> will always happen that lets him get out, no matter how many ridiculous coincidences have to happen together. This man is incredibly arrogant and attempts to use this power to toy with the Foundation to get what he wants – at least until he learns why the numebr-one rule of messing with the Foundation is, &quot;Don't.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative starts with an MTF being dispatched to Somerandomtown County (working name) to investigate reports of a prisoner in the county jail who's anomalously good at escaping. They track down the prisoner, tell him who they are, handcuff him, and take him to Site-8 for containment. After a week, a containment breach occurs at Site-8, letting him out. The MTF recaptures him, and the cycle of containment, escape, and recapture repeats as the Foundation creates harsher and harsher conprocs, until they figure out what's going on and decide to put out a reward for whoever can devise conprocs for this man. Eventually, the captain of the MTF, who at this point is sick of chasing this guy, asks him what the Foundation has to do to contain him. At this point, the guy starts making ridiculous demands to the tune of &quot;you have to contain me in a five-star hotel and give me anything I ask for, no matter how ridiculous-&quot; and then the captain just shoots him. Finally, the article ends with the SCP's updated containment file, with the class as Neutralized and the Special Containment Procedures being, &quot;If it doesn't comply, threaten lethal force.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Explores what would actually happen if the Foundation encountered an anomaly whose property is that he cannot be contained, and also tries to derive humor from some old Gary Stu cliches (&quot;my original chaructr is a humanid wat will DSTROIE EVERYSANG and BRETCH CONTEINMENT IF THE FONDANTION DOESNT GIV IT WHAT IT WANTS).</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>

