																		Re: (Seeking Greenlight) The Uncontainable Man
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609202346" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609120403 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Dec 2020 01:53</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855397">
									

<p>I'll be honest, I've seen lots of attempts at the same sort of premise. Most of the time the audience isn't much of a fan, especially if you're pairing the already arrogant overpowered main character with the Foundation being extremely incompetent (the situation you're describing in the narrative seems to necessitate an extreme waste of resources and personnel. It would make much more sense for the Foundation to either convince the guy that he wants to remain in whatever low-cost containment is reasonable for him, or just keep him rendered comatose 24/7).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: Explores what would actually happen if the Foundation encountered an anomaly whose property is that he cannot be contained</p>
</blockquote>
<p>We already have a lot of anomalies with similar properties. You can use the <a href="/tag-search">Tag Search</a> tool to search up the pages tagged with &quot;uncontained&quot;.</p>
<p>If you intend to focus on the comedic aspects of the Foundation being incompetent, I could potentially see this working as a tale, but the premise of curbstomping Mary Sues has already been addressed many times on the site, like in the Resurrection series where an agent shoots a reality bender, the joke article where Foundation personnel review and downvote a powerful anomalous being, tales like <a href="/eldritch-application">Eldritch Application</a>, and so on. You would need to have something significantly different and unique to make this stand out amongst the existing material.</p>

							</div>

								
					
