								<div class="title" id="post-title-4856088">
																		Re: (Seeking Greenlight) The Uncontainable Man
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/damian-thorne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7106669); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7106669&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609202346" alt="Damian Thorne" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7106669)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/damian-thorne" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7106669); return false;" >Damian Thorne</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609196971 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Dec 2020 23:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4856088">
									

<p>Thanks for the criticism. I still think that this can work, if I change the premise enough:</p>
<p>The &quot;Foundation being incompetent&quot; thing isn't a necessary part of the article, and can be rewritten by making our anomaly a <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5242">semiohazard</a>, a fact of the universe that shouldn't be true, but is. It's just a fact of baseline reality that this anomaly cannot be contained, just as it is a fact of baseline reality that &quot;The operations of 'YWTGTSYT' are perfectly legal.&quot; The overuse of resources and personnel is due to the fact that they can't get him to stay in containment for more than five minutes – and that also applies to the trucks they use to transport him. And while it would make more sense to convince the guy to remain in containment or keep him comatose, the first is not going to happen unless they threaten lethal force (which is what they figure out they have to do) for reasons discussed below, and the second counts as &quot;containment&quot; and thus will not work.</p>
<p>The character can also be reduced from an arrogant parody of Mary Sues to someone who really, <em>really</em> doesn't want to be locked up. He's had nightmares about it, he's always been terrified of it, and getting sentenced to prison confirmed all his worst fears about it. The causal link between this fear and the manifestation of his anomaly is unconfirmed; perhaps this was always a property of him, but it never became an issue until he was carted off to jail. Perhaps he manifested the property after going to jail.</p>
<p>Do you think that could work?</p>

							</div>

								
